# Clean Code: Design & Objects

## Prefer polymorphism over if/else chains

```php
// BAD
public function calculateDiscount(string $type): float
{
    if ($type === 'premium') return 0.2;
    elseif ($type === 'vip') return 0.3;
    else return 0;
}

// GOOD
enum MemberType: string {
    case Premium = 'premium';
    case Vip = 'vip';
    case Regular = 'regular';

    public function discount(): float
    {
        return match ($this) {
            self::Premium => 0.2,
            self::Vip => 0.3,
            self::Regular => 0,
        };
    }
}
```

## Use dependency injection

```php
// BAD
class OrderService {
    public function process(): void {
        $gateway = new StripeGateway();
    }
}

// GOOD
class OrderService {
    public function __construct(private PaymentGateway $gateway) {}
}
```

## Follow Law of Demeter - don't chain through objects

```php
// BAD
$city = $order->getCustomer()->getAddress()->getCity();

// GOOD
$city = $order->shippingCity();
```

## Hide internal structure

```php
// BAD
class Wallet {
    public float $balance = 0;
}
$wallet->balance += 100;

// GOOD
class Wallet {
    private float $balance = 0;
    public function deposit(float $amount): void { $this->balance += $amount; }
    public function getBalance(): float { return $this->balance; }
}
```

## Classes should be small and do one thing

```php
// BAD
class UserService {
    public function createUser() { ... }
    public function sendEmail() { ... }
    public function generateReport() { ... }
    public function processPayment() { ... }
}

// GOOD
class UserService { public function create(CreateUserData $data): User { ... } }
class NotificationService { public function sendWelcome(User $user): void { ... } }
```

## Keep few instance variables

## Base class should know nothing about derivatives

```php
// BAD
abstract class Payment {
    public function process(): void {
        if ($this instanceof CreditCardPayment) { ... }
    }
}

// GOOD
abstract class Payment {
    abstract public function process(): void;
}
```

## Prefer many focused functions over flag-based behavior

```php
// BAD
public function export(string $format): string { ... }

// GOOD
public function exportToPdf(): string { ... }
public function exportToCsv(): string { ... }
```

## Prefer non-static methods (testable, injectable)

```php
// BAD
class PriceCalculator {
    public static function calculate(float $price, float $tax): float { ... }
}

// GOOD
class PriceCalculator {
    public function calculate(float $price, float $tax): float { ... }
}
```

## Avoid hybrid structures (half object, half data)

```php
// BAD - exposes data AND has business logic
class User {
    public string $name;
    public string $email;
    public function sendWelcomeEmail(): void { ... }
}

// GOOD - either a DTO or an object with encapsulation
class UserData { public function __construct(public string $name, public string $email) {} }
class UserService { public function sendWelcomeEmail(UserData $user): void { ... } }
```

## Prevent over-configurability - keep configurable data at high levels

```php
// BAD - config scattered in deep logic
private function calculateShipping(): float {
    $rate = env('SHIPPING_RATE', 0.05);
}

// GOOD - config injected from top level
public function __construct(private float $shippingRate) {}
```
